# Koine Greek — Pimsleur Audio Course

90 audio lessons (16.7 hours) teaching ~600 Koine Greek words covering ~90% of the NT text, using the Pimsleur method (anticipation, graduated interval recall) set in 1st century Palestine.

## Levels

| Level | Lessons | Hours | Words | NT Coverage |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 — Ὁ Ξένος | 1-30 | ~5.5 | ~200 | ~75% |
| 2 — Ὁ Μαθητής | 31-60 | ~5.5 | ~400 | ~85% |
| 3 — Ὁ Κήρυξ | 61-90 | ~5.7 | ~600 | ~90% |

## Usage

```bash
source venv/bin/activate

# Generate a single lesson
python -m src.generate --lesson 5

# Generate a range
python -m src.generate --range 1 10

# Generate all
python -m src.generate --all

# Enrich lesson scripts with LLM (uses koine-anki data)
python src/enrich.py kiro-test/lesson_01_script.json

# Generate Anki decks from lessons
python src/generate_decks.py

# Serve audio to phone
python serve_audio.py
```

## Dependencies

- **koine-anki** (sibling repo) — provides NT corpus, Strong's dictionary, and morphology data for enriching lesson scripts. Set `KOINE_ANKI_PATH` env var or place repos as siblings.

## Tech Stack

- **Spanish narration**: Amazon Polly (Mia, es-MX, neural)
- **Greek speech**: Google Cloud TTS (Chirp3-HD + Wavenet-B fallback)
- **Audio assembly**: Python (pydub + ffmpeg)
- **Anki generation**: genanki
- **LLM enrichment**: Amazon Bedrock (Claude)

## Setup

```bash
python3 -m venv venv && source venv/bin/activate
pip install genanki py-sblgnt google-cloud-texttospeech boto3 pydub
brew install ffmpeg
```

## Project Structure

```
├── audio/              90 lesson MP3s organized by level
├── src/
│   ├── engine.py           Audio generation engine
│   ├── tts.py              TTS module (Polly + Google)
│   ├── generate.py         Lesson generator
│   ├── render.py           MP3 renderer
│   ├── script_builder.py   Script generator
│   ├── enrich.py           LLM enrichment (uses koine-anki data)
│   ├── generate_decks.py   Anki deck generator from lessons
│   └── data/               Lesson content (90 lessons)
├── decks/              Generated outputs (.apkg, .mp3)
├── notes/              Curriculum and lessons learned
└── serve_audio.py      HTTP server for phone playback
```
